Description: Kidux's installer, for the live system of Kidux's image
 Kidux is a Debian derivative for a child's first computer. This package is
 the installer of its image: Calamares, with Kidux's settings and look,
 started full screen in place of Kidux's sign-in screen when the image's
 live system starts. It copies the live system, a Kidux machine already, to
 the computer's disk, with the system and /home on partitions of their own,
 and the administrator's account.
 .
 It belongs in the image's live system alone: the installer takes it off the
 system it installs. Installing it on a Kidux machine would replace the
 sign-in screen with the installer at the next start of a live system only,
 and change nothing else.
